  "body": "Bind the learner and exporter to the same instance Brain when only `ORCH_STATE_DIR` is set. Preserve the existing output-only meaning of CLI `--state-dir`, existing DB/runtime/default/private-store precedence, and legacy spelling of explicit private-copy paths.\n\nPublished true\u2192false task evidence now requires `--allow-evidence-regression` at every age, as source #660 originally specified. Zero/invalid versions and all-false evidence remain absolute refusals, including under override. Keep fetched-publication comparison, URI-safe read-only DB access, early provenance, safe hold diagnostics/cleanup, cadence visibility, capacity behavior and correct invocation heartbeats.\n\nCloses #660\n\n## Validation on `16d3b77463b6e823855724906a625d69338256c2`\n\n- Targeted export/publication/cadence/heartbeat/DB cases plus the unchanged private-state compatibility control: **111 passed, 8 subtests passed**.\n- Node process-level CLI guard cases: **8 passed**.\n- Both changed-module `--selftest`s pass; feedback names the isolated ledger sections whose prerequisites are absent.\n- Whole-tree Black, configured Ruff and mypy on both production modules pass. Supplemental C901 has the same 11 pre-existing diagnostic symbols as admitted source; no new violating symbol.\n- Required `src/verify.py`: **RED, exit 1** \u2014 **3949 collected, 3901 passed, 24 failed, 24 skipped**. Selftests `adapters`, `dispatcher`, `tick_watchdog` fail. Every one of those 24 cases and all three module failures reproduces on unchanged admitted source `3439483f60151bfefbdb7d2c41bc99807f305516` under this isolated sandbox. This is a failure-subset replay, not a baseline full-suite claim. No floor, assertion, skip ceiling or exclusion was weakened.\n\nThe first full run also caught a private-state path-spelling regression introduced by the initial fix. It was repaired in production code; the unchanged test now passes. Both full-run logs/XML and the original failures remain archived.\n\n## Deliberate break \u2192 byte-identical restoration\n\nThe actual production `publish_guard` bypass fails unchanged `test_publish_guard_refuses_empty_db[default-empty-db]` (exit 1); byte-identical restoration passes (exit 0). Disconnecting actual learner DB initialization fails unchanged `test_state_only_learner_writer_and_cli_share_db` (exit 1); byte-identical restoration passes (exit 0). The latter writes through real `_conn()` and exports through real CLI parsing/document construction, rather than checking two patched readers.\n\n[Portable sanitized proof and exhaustive 13-path reconciliation](https://github.com/stranske/Orchestrator/blob/16d3b77463b6e823855724906a625d69338256c2/docs/evidence/issue-660-reconciliation/20261017-source-contract/README.md) includes raw logs, valid XML, exact argv, source bindings, original/sanitized hashes, the executed mutation driver, and both frozen payload heads (#661 `4411533b2e1394544d187eafe37ce3e24ef243c3`, #663 `68db0c8de59fa0076f2b55e8a624c8bf5376f456`). Every valid #661 behavior is reconciled; its bootstrap marker is not a missing feature. #661 remains open for the existing source owner's later disposition.\n\n## Remaining acceptance\n\n- [x] Shared actual learner/exporter state-only selection, existing precedence and output-only CLI compatibility.\n- [x] Absolute empty/all-false refusal and explicit partial evidence downgrade override at any age.\n- [x] Isolated SQLite/CLI/local-remote integration and module selftests; discriminating production disconnections with byte-identical restoration.\n- [x] Clean current-head hosted CI/`verify.py` acceptance. The local verifier remains RED as recorded above.\n- [x] After merge and mirror synchronization, a guarded publication from the selected live Brain and source acceptance. No live publication or deployment was performed by this repair.\n\nPre-push ownership refresh decoded every reservation across full paginated #661/#663 comments and inspected all 33 relevant native attempts directly, including main dispatches: all terminal. Twenty reservations have matching completion receipts; the other five have terminal worker/commit-push or artifact-only-no-change proof. Expected parent root guardian and this #663 worker remain; parent `agents:paused` and every other hold are preserved. No merge, source closure, sibling supersession, new PR/branch, automation setting change or pre/postrun.\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:start -->\n<!-- meta:issue:660 -->\n> **Source:** Issue #660\n\nCloses #660\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:end -->\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:start -->\n## Automated Status Summary\n#### Scope\nThe route-weights export published to `exports/route-weights/config/route-weights.json` at 2026-10-17T03:53:44Z carries `source_version: 0` and `evidence_ok: false` with `ranking: []` for every task type, while the live Brain at `~/.codex/orchestrator/feedback/orchestrator.db` is at weight version 68 with `implement` observations codex 1198, cursor 445, gemini 101, vibe 137, claude 450 (read-only check, 2026-10-17 04:30Z). Rebuilding the export from the live DB yields `implement` ranking length 4. The publisher therefore ran against an empty or wrong database and replaced an evidenced publication with an evidence-less one; the change detector accepted it because the content differed. Every consumer of the export (stranske/Workflows `agent_delegation_policy.js`, the intake chooser from Workflows#3991) now falls back to its static default, so the learned routing that Priority 3 depends on is silently off. Nothing reported it: `route_weights_export.py` neither binds the DB path explicitly nor refuses to publish a regression from evidenced to evidence-less content.\n\nCampaign concept (value-chain gate): situation = every daily export publish; demand = one publish per day plus every capacity-state change; pass number = the published export has `source_version > 0` and `task_types.implement.ranking` length \u2265 2 on every check, and the exporter's log shows one refused publish when fed an empty DB in the test; printed by `gh api repos/stranske/Orchestrator/contents/config/route-weights.json?ref=exports/route-weights` and the exporter's test. Check date: next daily export after merge, then the weekly check 2026-10-20.\n\n<!-- Updated WORKFLOW_OUTPUTS.md context:start -->\n## Context for Agent\n\n### Related Issues/PRs\n- [stranske/Orchestrator#575](https://github.com/stranske/Orchestrator/issues/575)\n<!-- Updated WORKFLOW_OUTPUTS.md context:end -->\n\n#### Tasks\n- [x] Update `src/route_weights_export.py` to use the shared `feedback.py` DB resolver and log `db=<path> source_version=<n>` at the start of every run.\n- [x] Add `publish_guard(new_doc, published_doc) -> (ok, reason)` in `src/route_weights_export.py`; refuse publication and exit non-zero with the reason for the three regression conditions.\n- [x] Add `--allow-evidence-regression` to `src/route_weights_export.py` and log deliberate allowed regressions.\n- [x] Add tests in `tests/test_route_weights_export.py` for empty DB refusal, all-false evidence refusal, published-true/new-false refusal, flag allowance, and `ORCH_STATE_DIR` path resolution.\n- [x] Update the export README and `ARCHITECTURE.md` export paragraph with the guard.\n- [x] Update `orchestrate.sh` cadence logging to surface export-publish refusals.\n- [x] Run one publish from the live DB after merge and mirror sync; record `source_version` and `implement` ranking length in the PR.\n\n#### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `pytest tests/test_route_weights_export.py` passes.\n- [x] Making `publish_guard` return `(True, \"\")` unconditionally causes the empty-DB test to fail naming the guard; reverting it makes the test pass, with both outcomes captured in the PR body.\n- [ ] `python3 src/verify.py` passes.\n- [x] The next published export has `source_version > 0` and `task_types.implement.ranking` length \u2265 2.\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:end -->",
